# Kwetu shell UI strings — Swahili (Kiswahili) locale.
# Source of truth: gettext PO (docs/swahili-i18n.md §2). msgid is the English
# source string; msgctxt carries the screen path (<screen>/, snake_case,
# trailing slash). Placeholders are i18next tokens {{token}}, never printf.
#
# EVERY sw msgstr below carries the `#, fuzzy` flag: these are agent-drafted
# renderings (docs/swahili-i18n.md §1.4) pending the native-speaker review
# gate. Nothing here is approved sw copy yet.
#
# Term notes for the reviewer (draft renderings, per the §8 glossary seed):
#   Play → Cheza, Settings → Mipangilio, Continue → Endelea, Stop → Simama,
#   Sound/Audio → Sauti, Players → Wachezaji, Scroll → Jonga (verify against
#   "sogeza"; TUKI glosses "jonga" as gaze/stare), Mute → Nyamazisha.
#   "Jumuishia" (suggested for the UI set) does not fit any shell string in
#   this file and was left out rather than forced — glossary item.
#   "Ping" is left as a loanword.
#
# Compiled with tools/spikes/s0.10/i18n/compile.mjs (i18next-conv CLI + contract
# normalizer) to locales/sw/translation.json.
